LibreHVI-CIDNet includes code adapted from HVI-CIDNet:

Source: https://github.com/Fediory/HVI-CIDNet
Commit: eb43d7d91e9a336c66856824ff9e4603ae41f408
License: MIT
Copyright (c) 2024 Fediory Feng

The inference port covers net/CIDNet.py, net/HVI_transform.py, net/LCA.py,
and net/transformer_utils.py. Module and parameter names mirror the upstream
network. The upstream MIT einops rearrangements are expressed with equivalent
native PyTorch reshape operations; training, losses, metrics, and dataset code
are not included.

Source path behaviorally referenced: eval_hf.py (RGB [0,1] preprocessing,
right/bottom reflection padding to a multiple of 8, gamma/control application,
output clamping, and crop to the original canvas). The family helper is a
native implementation rather than a copy of that file.

